    <title>Some remarks on Quillen's Dévissage theorem</title>
    <updated>2025-05-28T19:03:20Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2505.13260v2" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2505.13260v2" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>In this paper we give a different proof of Quillen's Dévissage theorem using Barwick's theorem of the heart. The key ingredient is a certain short exact sequence of dg categories, which is closely related with the Auslander-type construction for nilpotent extensions which was used in the papers of Kuznetsov-Lunts \cite{KL15}, Land-Tamme \cite{LT19} and the author \cite{E20}.</summary>
